WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.993 --> 00:00:10.911
Hi, I’m Evan Carmichael.

00:00:11.141 --> 00:00:12.576
Welcome to another edition of Ask Evan.

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:14.361
Today’s question comes from one of my

00:00:14.361 --> 00:00:15.877
forum readers Anthony

00:00:15.877 --> 00:00:17.293
who wrote in asking about business plan

00:00:17.725 --> 00:00:19.328
and he said, “Is a good business plan

00:00:19.554 --> 00:00:21.911
the first thing that you need to do to start a business.”

00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:25.347
As much of a fan of business plans that I am Anthony

00:00:25.347 --> 00:00:26.248
and thank you for the question

00:00:26.249 --> 00:00:28.461
I think a lot of people go through that question as well

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.397
I don’t think it’s the first thing that you should do

00:00:31.506 --> 00:00:33.854
and the reason being, when you’re creating your business plan

00:00:34.158 --> 00:00:36.677
you should really have a good sense of your market

00:00:36.906 --> 00:00:39.304
and what you’re going to do to create your product

00:00:39.304 --> 00:00:40.323
and service and sell it.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:42.801
In the early stages of a business

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:44.262
what you really need to do

00:00:44.452 --> 00:00:46.103
is start talking to customers to figure out

00:00:46.381 --> 00:00:48.009
what kind of business you should launch

00:00:48.832 --> 00:00:50.466
and the best type of business you can launch

00:00:50.757 --> 00:00:52.922
is building around your customers.

00:00:53.225 --> 00:00:55.055
So you go start talking to potential customers.

00:00:55.312 --> 00:00:57.213
Find out what their problems are their pain points

00:00:57.413 --> 00:01:00.993
and try to develop a solution that can help them.

00:01:01.425 --> 00:01:03.425
We made this mistake, one of my earlier companies

00:01:04.252 --> 00:01:07.137
we spent an entire summer drafting a business plan

00:01:07.213 --> 00:01:08.362
that we thought was awesome

00:01:08.362 --> 00:01:09.511
and of course our customers

00:01:09.511 --> 00:01:10.661
are going to want this product

00:01:11.148 --> 00:01:12.952
and this is, you know, the best thing ever

00:01:13.118 --> 00:01:14.474
and we spent so much time researching

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.017
and figured we had the best thing

00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:18.140
but then when we, you know

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.355
got to actually launching it turns out that the customer

00:01:21.562 --> 00:01:23.484
we’re going after didn’t really care

00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:24.512
or give us the time of day.

00:01:24.803 --> 00:01:27.240
Now luckily we had, you know, enough still in our product

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.303
to make it successful and we would find other customers

00:01:29.341 --> 00:01:32.621
but we spent all this time creating this business plan

00:01:32.621 --> 00:01:33.617
that we thought was amazing

00:01:34.342 --> 00:01:36.545
and then when we went out to actually test it in the market

00:01:36.723 --> 00:01:39.437
we found out that it didn’t hold any water.

00:01:39.704 --> 00:01:41.433
So the best thing that you can do in the beginning

00:01:41.624 --> 00:01:42.551
when you’re first starting your business

00:01:42.854 --> 00:01:44.114
or you’re thinking about starting a business

00:01:44.484 --> 00:01:46.133
is go start talking to customers

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:47.795
and they’ll tell you what they need

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.721
what they like, how you can help them

00:01:49.993 --> 00:01:52.141
and from there you’ll get the information you need

00:01:52.251 --> 00:01:53.528
to be able to create your business plan.

00:01:53.966 --> 00:01:55.400
The danger doing it to the other way

00:01:55.741 --> 00:01:58.129
is your business plan will be, you know

00:01:58.324 --> 00:02:00.097
useless and extinct, you know

00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:01.961
the day you actually start going out and marketing your product.

00:02:02.241 --> 00:02:03.240
As you launch your business

00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:04.897
your business plan is going to change.

00:02:05.042 --> 00:02:05.960
You’re going to get new opportunities

00:02:06.157 --> 00:02:07.525
customers will come to you with new problems

00:02:07.722 --> 00:02:09.011
your marketing strategy will change

00:02:09.354 --> 00:02:10.613
your expenses might change a little bit.

00:02:11.307 --> 00:02:13.841
So your business plan will constantly have to change a little bit

00:02:14.405 --> 00:02:17.553
but it’s best if you can to have a good concept

00:02:17.553 --> 00:02:20.588
from the beginning built around what you know will sell

00:02:20.588 --> 00:02:21.508
and what customers want.

00:02:22.062 --> 00:02:25.028
So my number one thing if you’re starting a business

00:02:25.226 --> 00:02:26.953
is just go start talking to customers.

00:02:27.486 --> 00:02:28.260
Find out their problems

00:02:28.486 --> 00:02:30.069
build a solution around their needs

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:32.895
and then once you’ve got a sense of what their challenges are

00:02:33.121 --> 00:02:34.512
and you’re able to get a couple of orders

00:02:34.512 --> 00:02:36.997
ideally coming in you can create your business plan

00:02:36.997 --> 00:02:38.854
on how you’re going to create this, you know

00:02:39.098 --> 00:02:40.744
company out of this idea

00:02:41.021 --> 00:02:43.574
and be able to go out and expand to other companies

00:02:43.813 --> 00:02:46.493
build a team, build your facilities if you need to

00:02:46.763 --> 00:02:48.024
and continue to grow the business.

00:02:48.495 --> 00:02:49.918
So hopefully that helps Anthony.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.948
For those of you watching, if you liked the video

00:02:52.126 --> 00:02:52.948
please give it a thumbs-up.

00:02:53.155 --> 00:02:54.352
I always love seeing those come in.

00:02:54.612 --> 00:02:56.241
And if you have a thought for Anthony

00:02:56.406 --> 00:02:58.032
or you have a question I’d love to hear it

00:02:58.249 --> 00:02:59.633
if you want to leave a comment underneath the video.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.216
So thank you and we’ll see you on the next episode.

